  "worked_solution": "Since $∠AOD$ is a straight angle, the angles $∠AOE$ and $∠DOE$ are supplementary. Two angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the measure of the angle $∠AOE$ that's supplementary to the angle of $∠DOE=5x-{5}^{∘}$ must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOE & ={180}^{∘}-(5x-5)^{∘} \\\\  & =({180}^{∘}+{5}^{∘})-5{x}^{∘} \\\\  & ={(185-5x)}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
